The project investigates p22phox (encoded by the CYBA gene) and the p.Q143* nonsense mutation, which introduces a premature stop codon after position 142 and truncates the 195-amino-acid protein. Using interactive py3Dmol molecular models and schematic visualizations, the project illustrates how losing the C-terminal region removes a key binding interface for p47phox, impairing activation of the NADPH oxidase complex and its catalytic core (NOX2), reducing the antimicrobial respiratory burst, and linking to chronic granulomatous disease (CGD). It also models the healthy activation mechanism in which phosphorylation of the p47phox C-terminus exposes its SH3 domain to bind p22phox.
